<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baldwin II, Margrave of Flanders</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 865–918</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Baldwin II of Flanders, Baldwin the Bald</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baldwin II, called the Bald, was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> from 879 to 918, son of Baldwin I Iron Arm and Judith, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>. Using the disorder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raids, he built fortresses and gathered counties, abbeys and royal lands into a single principality. He married Ælfthryth, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a>, and divided his lands between his sons Arnulf I and Adalulf.</p></div>
